  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: DiscRC 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "While your lab is exploring new treatment ideas for cancer, you keep
    careful records about which ideas are showing the most promise and help prepare
    reports that may later support preclinical studies.\n\n<b>Research coordinators
    create and test new treatment ideas in the lab to make sure they\u2019re safe
    for people.</b>\n\nIs this <b>true</b> or <b>false</b>?"
  explanation: "Research coordinators don\u2019t create or test new drugs themselves.
    During the early drug discovery stage\u2014before any lab or animal studies begin\u2014they
    help organize research plans, manage samples and records, and ensure all required
    approvals and ethical guidelines are in place. By handling these behind-the-scenes
    details early on, they support researchers so discovery work can move forward
    smoothly and responsibly."
  correctAnswer: False
  incorrectAnswer1: True
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Research Coordinator
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
